# /home/tunnel/.ssh/authorized_keys  (example — do NOT commit real keys)
#
# Each line is one public key with options that restrict what the key may do.
# Replace <YOUR_PUBLIC_KEY> with the actual key string and <KEY_COMMENT> with
# a meaningful label (e.g. "laptop-2025", "workstation-alice").
#
# KEY OPTION REFERENCE:
#   restrict             — deny all features not explicitly re-enabled below
#   permitopen="H:P"     — allow local port-forwarding only to host H on port P
#   from="IP/CIDR"       — restrict key use to connections originating from that IP
#   command="CMD"        — force execution of CMD instead of any requested command
#   no-pty               — prevent interactive PTY allocation
#   no-agent-forwarding  — prevent SSH agent forwarding
#   no-X11-forwarding    — prevent X11 forwarding
#
# CLIENT USAGE EXAMPLE (forward Apache for local inspection, no shell):
#   ssh -N -l tunnel <VPS_PUBLIC_IP> -L 8080:<CONTAINER_IP>:8080
#   # Then browse: http://localhost:8080/

# ── Example 1: forward to Apache only (no source-IP restriction) ──────────────
# Use this when your workstation IP changes (e.g. laptop on dynamic IP).

no-pty,no-agent-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,restrict,permitopen="<CONTAINER_IP>:8080" <YOUR_PUBLIC_KEY> <KEY_COMMENT>

# ── Example 2: forward to Apache, restricted to a specific source IP ──────────
# Preferred when your admin workstation has a static/known IP.
# Replace <ADMIN_SOURCE_IP> with e.g. 203.0.113.10 or 203.0.113.0/24

# from="<ADMIN_SOURCE_IP>",no-pty,no-agent-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,restrict,permitopen="<CONTAINER_IP>:8080" <YOUR_PUBLIC_KEY> <KEY_COMMENT>

# ── Example 3: forward + force nologin command (belt-and-suspenders) ──────────
# Explicitly prevents any interactive shell even if sshd configuration changes.

# command="/usr/sbin/nologin",no-pty,no-agent-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,restrict,permitopen="<CONTAINER_IP>:8080" <YOUR_PUBLIC_KEY> <KEY_COMMENT>

# ── Example 4: second key for a different operator (different target port) ────

# no-pty,no-agent-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,restrict,permitopen="<CONTAINER_IP>:8080" <YOUR_SECOND_PUBLIC_KEY> <SECOND_KEY_COMMENT>
